  GREEN  GSRCPIN          his instrument read at SRC_PIN 268457d1 is byte-identical to the one on origin/main (feee11ab3a2c vs feee11ab3a2c) — the key is not stale relative to the subject. His subject pin 0ae48068 predates his own unit, so the instrument cannot be read there at all
  GREEN  GLIFT            his keys lifted from unit-464presc-2026-11-03/census-presc.mjs + his own LIFTS table at 0ae48068: LIFTS(10L) SELECTOR_WIDE(6L) MOVABLE_WIDE(7L) KP_TEXT(5L) closedTextOf(23L) · upstream [blankNonCode lineOf IDIOMS spans enclosingIf declarationsOf KIND_AXISB kindOf] · SELECTOR_WIDE 4 arms · MOVABLE_WIDE 5 arms · selector kinds [selector] movable kinds [live,run-derived]
  GREEN  GKPINSPANPOS     BLOCKING: a constructed predicate with both anchor literals INLINED is accepted by his in-span filter: sel=true mov=true both=true. The filter can fire
  GREEN  GKPINSPANNEG     the matched negative — same predicate, the movable anchor replaced by a pinned rev — is NOT in-span for movable (sel=true mov=false), so the arm is not firing on everything
  GREEN  GKPINSPAN        his own blocking KP, the one his §3 exists to make the zero mean something, reads both-in-span=false (sel false · mov false) when its predicate line is put through the in-span filter — while the SAME text through the candidate arm reads sel true · mov true. The filter that publishes "0 of 11" has no known positive
  GREEN  GDIFFFILTER      his wide selector arm matches an ADDING-commit read as if it were a recency selector: `--diff-filter=A ... .pop()` on a newest-first list is the OLDEST entry and is stable, yet SELECTOR_WIDE arms [3] match it (the real recency line matches arms [0,3]). So GSTALEPIN is a FALSE POSITIVE of the selector arm, not an artifact of the expansion's reach
  GREEN  GINSPANBASE      tree-wide, over 670 leg sites and not only the 11 candidates, the in-span conjunction holds 0 times (0.0%): selector-in-span 3, movable-in-span 11, either 14. A filter whose positive rate over the whole tree is 0.0% is measuring the tree's hoisted-operand coding style, not the ordering
  GREEN  GRESOLVEONLY     every one of the 11 candidates reaches at least one of its two anchors ONLY after identifier resolution — 11 of 11. The candidate arm resolves bindings; the in-span filter does not, so no candidate in a hoisted-operand tree can pass it
  GREEN  GWHYARM          1 of 11 candidates carry an anchor that is in the why-string arm and NOT in the boolean operand: [GTUPLE sel]. A why-string is not a conjunct. His `prose-arg-call` flag caught one shape of this; the arm split measures it per candidate
  GREEN  GBOOLPAIR        with the BOOLEAN OPERAND resolved on its own — which is how a predicate actually carries its anchors — 8 of 11 candidates hold a selector anchor beside a movable anchor: [GTARGET · GFIXEDCTRL · GTUPLE · GTARGETB · GSTALEPIN · GSTALE · GSTALEINVERT · C3b]. His stated necessary property is satisfied 8 times in this tree, not 0. The "0" is his in-span filter's figure, and that filter has no known positive (GKPINSPAN)
  GREEN  GHANDCOVER       the filed hand read covers exactly the candidate set this drive enumerated: 11 rows against 11 candidates, every id matched member by member
  GREEN  GBRACKET         THE BRACKET: his published 0 is a FLOOR (in-span, keyed on anchor literals, no known positive) and my 8 is a CEILING (unbounded resolution reaches a run record's whole harness). Neither endpoint decides the label. By hand over all 11 candidates — 6 read by me this fire, 5 his reading recorded as his — legs whose boolean operand carries BOTH anchors: 2 [GSTALE · GSTALEINVERT]; legs that are a CONJUNCT PAIR with disagreeing figures: 0. So the prescription label HOLDS, and it holds on the hand read, not on either instrument's figure
  GREEN  GWHYARMR         why-only at the IDENTIFIER level: 3 of 11 candidates reach an anchor from the resolved why arm and not from the resolved boolean arm [U4 sel · GC2MOVED mov · GHISTFLIP sel]
  GREEN  GREPRO           my reconstruction of his in-span filter reproduces his published per-candidate figures off his own recording: 11 of 11 rows agree on (id, sel-in-span, mov-in-span), and my candidate set is 11 against his 11
